 "observations": [
  "body L1-L3: rule (β) is checked: it is the last formula of p. 188 solved for sin m; with tg for the trigonometric tangent, sin φ / cos φ, Ḥabash's R tg φ tg δ is the same, for the radius 1 the modern sin m = tg φ tg δ.",
  "body L5, L14, L25: the heads of the notes on chapters 14, 15 and 16, «Ad» and «caput» in small capitals, in the larger type of the heads.",
  "body L6, L15, L26: in the heads, the dashes after «a)» measure 10.4, 10.1 and 9.7 pt and the dash of «29–30» 5.4 pt; transcribed as dashes and a long dash.",
  "body L8: a spot of ink stands on the first a of «aequatoris»; it is not a sign.",
  "body L9, L11, L20, L23, L24: the minus signs are printed as long dashes (9.6 to 10.2 pt); they are set as minus signs.",
  "body L8-L13, L18-L24: the rules are checked. In a northern latitude the zenith distance of the Sun at noon is φ − δ, the declination δ counted positive to the north, so that altit. merid. = 90° − φ + δ: with the Sun north of the equator φ = 90° − (altit. merid. − declinat.), rule (α) of chapter 14, and with the Sun south, its declination taken positive, φ = 90° − (altit. merid. + declinat.), rule (β); together φ = complem. altit. merid. ± declinat. Rules (α), (α′), (β) and (β′) of chapter 15 are the same relations solved for the meridian altitude.",
  "body L18, L33: the dashes of the letter-spaced «al–Battānī» measure 5.4 pt, long dashes.",
  "body L30: a speck stands after «meridiem»; it is not a full stop."
 ],
